  "schema": "ancora.parity.scenario.v1",
  "id": "s11-shared-resources",
  "title": "Shared resources (D9d): other resources, resource groups, the resources generar() gives, continuation",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D9d (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-057..059; SQL case 142). One plan with two periods (2 days x 3 slots each), one run per period: run W1 first, then run W2, which continues from W1's placements and resource uses.",
    "Legacy side: the resources through add_OtroRecurso; the resource window of each template: add_OtroGrupoDeRecursosParaActividad (priority 1, needed 1, essential), get_form_add_rxact for the hidden max_prioridad, one add_OtroRecursoParaActividad per checked resource, custom_set_PrioridadRxact and set_GrupoRecursos_imprescindibles on the template's LAST group only (an UPDATE moves a row to the end of the table, and generar() reads the groups in physical order, D18). Drupal side: SharedResources, the saves of the template's resource editor.",
    "generar() gives each placed activity resources from every group of its template except the last one, ordered by resource priority, then use, then travel cost (case 142). Run W1: Group 1 gets R1 and Group 2 gets R2 (R1 is then used once). Run W2 (group {R2, R4}): with the uses of run W1 loaded, Group 1 gets R4 (R2 is used once) and Group 2 gets R2 (a tie, physical order); without them it would be R2 and R4. The workspace round trip therefore shows that the published resource uses are loaded into the next workspace."
  ],
